Author: Lauri Ahonen <ahonjoonas@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 09:28:48 2026 +0300

    Land the observability work and cap read_output at 6,000 characters
    
    Two changes in one commit because they overlap inside process-manager.ts and
    server.ts; splitting them would mean partial-file surgery on code that tests
    green as a unit.
    
    Observability (uncommitted since this morning, now landed): per-call caller_id,
    transport telemetry, the process-receipt store, the mcp_status / process_state /
    elapsed_ms / next_action envelope on start_process and read_output, bounded
    read waits, the process-guard and transport-telemetry test suites, and the
    view_image contract stating model-only inspection with no user-chat delivery.
    
    Cap: read_output drops from 20,000 to 6,000 characters per stream. Measured
    2026-08-25, payloads of 6.4 KB were delivered while 12.8 KB and 14.4 KB were
    blocked by the platform safety layer after the process had already run to
    exit 0 -- so the old cap produced an invisible failure, with the output sitting
    complete in the receipt while the caller saw only a safety error and no
    truncation marker. At 6,000 the same read truncates visibly and sets
    stdout_truncated, so callers page the rest instead of losing it.
    
    npm test passes: telemetry, process guard, OAuth retention, concurrency 4/4,
    and live smoke against the restarted listener reporting the exact seven tools.

